We apply the distributive property repeatedly:

\begin{align*}
(x+10)(2y+10) &= x(2y+10) + 10(2y+10)\\
&= x\cdot 2y + x\cdot 10 + 10\cdot 2y + 10\cdot 10\\
&= \boxed{2xy + 10x + 20y + 100}.
\end{align*}

We can write $f(x)$ as follows:
\[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x^2 & \text{if $x > 0$}, \\
0 & \text{if $x = 0$}, \\
-x^2 & \text{if $x < 0$}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Hence, $f^{-1}(4) + f^{-1}(-100) = 2 + (-10) = \boxed{-8}.$

